  "interpretation": "Four preregistered tournaments completed over 120 fresh source groups (3,600 correlated variants). In cycle one the frozen gate scores -0.420 at baseline and +0.373 with 200ms added delay: reduced tail loss offsets lower mean P&L, but the paired mean-change interval includes zero. The positive-score rule then selected 400ms on a disjoint cohort, where the gate scores -0.079. Neither model nor threshold was changed; no champion was promoted. These directed synthetic results do not establish general latency robustness or a break-even frontier.",
